# Release-archive exclusions (`git archive`, and therefore GitHub's "Source code"
# tarballs, honour `export-ignore`).
#
# `packaging/` is excluded because `packaging/daer.plan.toml` pins the SHA-256 of the
# release tarball it is used to build. If the plan were inside that tarball, the digest
# would have to describe a file containing itself, and there is no fixed point — so the
# package could never verify its own source. Excluding the directory makes the digest
# computable, and it is the honest boundary anyway: a build recipe is not an input to the
# build it describes. (The value still cannot be committed, because `git archive` embeds the
# commit SHA in the archive's pax header; the plan explains why and names the recipe that
# fills it in at package-build time.) `docs/`, `crates/` and `ebpf/` stay in: the package
# compiles and reads them.
packaging/ export-ignore
